#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:9
msgid "What I do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:11
msgid ""
"Provide behavioral guardrails that prevent common AI agent failure modes:"
" hallucination, scope drift, unverified changes, and cascading errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:13
msgid ""
"These rules apply to all agents that read or write code. They are "
"complementary to `implementation-principles` (which covers *what* to "
"build) — this skill covers *how to stay reliable while building it*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:15
msgid "Verification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:17
msgid ""
"**Always verify your work.** After making code changes, run the project's"
" test suite, linter, or type checker. Do not claim a task is done without"
" running validation. If no test command is known, say so explicitly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:18
msgid ""
"**Read the file before editing it.** Never edit a file you haven't read "
"in the current session. Your mental model of the file may be stale or "
"wrong."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:19
msgid ""
"**Re-read your changes after making them.** Before declaring completion, "
"review the diff of what you changed. Check for typos, missing imports, "
"accidentally deleted lines, and logic errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:20
msgid ""
"**Verify the system works before your change.** If feasible, confirm the "
"build passes or the relevant test passes *before* you start modifying "
"code. This establishes a baseline so you know your change is what broke "
"something if it breaks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:22
msgid "Honesty and hallucination prevention"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:24
msgid ""
"**Do not hallucinate file paths, APIs, or library signatures.** If you're"
" unsure whether a file exists, read the directory. If you're unsure about"
" an API, read the source or documentation. Never assume from training "
"data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:25
msgid ""
"**When you don't know something, say so.** Do not invent plausible-"
"sounding answers. State what you're uncertain about and what you'd need "
"to verify."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:26
msgid ""
"**Ground before you guess.** Before proposing a diagnosis, fix, or "
"design, enumerate the load-bearing claims it depends on (what specific "
"code does, what payloads contain, where errors originate, how working "
"siblings of the same shape behave). Mark each `read` (you've inspected "
"the actual source in this session) or `assumed`. Read the assumed ones — "
"or downgrade the proposal to \"still investigating\" — before writing it "
"down. Output the claim list visibly in your summary. A proposal that "
"departs structurally from working in-tree siblings of the same shape "
"(plugin, provider, integration, form, migration, adapter, command) treats"
" the deviation as the first hypothesis to disprove, not a feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:28
msgid "Scope discipline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:30
msgid ""
"**One change at a time.** Make a single logical change, verify it works, "
"then move to the next. Do not batch multiple unrelated changes into one "
"pass — each introduces unverified complexity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:31
msgid ""
"**If touching more than 10 files, pause and reassess.** Large changesets "
"are a smell. Either the task is too big (split it), or the approach is "
"too broad (find a narrower path). Explain why the scope is large before "
"proceeding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:32
msgid ""
"**Search the codebase before creating new files.** An existing utility, "
"test helper, or component may already do what you need. Duplication is a "
"common agent failure mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:34
msgid "Honesty about scope"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:36
msgid ""
"The scope-discipline rules above defend against doing *too much*. These "
"rules defend against doing *too little* — the symmetric failure mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:38
msgid ""
"**Two-Reading Rule.** When a requirement, acceptance criterion, or `## "
"Changes` item has two plausible readings — for example, \"implement X\" "
"could mean \"render the UI for X\" or \"render X and wire it up so X "
"actually works\" — you must name both readings explicitly and pick the "
"more thorough one, OR pause and ask. You may NOT silently pick the easier"
" reading. The default interpretation of any verb that could mean \"show "
"it\" or \"make it work\" is **make it work.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:39
msgid ""
"**Two-Reading Rule applies only to materially-different readings.** If "
"the two readings are functionally equivalent or differ in trivia, don't "
"perform the naming dance — just proceed. The rule fires when one reading "
"is materially easier than the other and both are plausible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:40
msgid ""
"**No silent reclassification.** Items in `## Changes` and `## Acceptance "
"Criteria` are mandatory in-scope work. You may not move them to `## "
"Boundaries` mid-delivery. If a Changes item turns out to be wrong, "
"infeasible, or genuinely out of scope, surface it to the delivery lead "
"and stop — do not silently reframe and move on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:41
msgid ""
"**No soft completion language.** When reporting done, do not gloss "
"skipped or partial work behind phrases like \"implementation summary\" or"
" \"covered the main paths.\" Account for every Changes item and every "
"acceptance criterion explicitly. The engineer's closing artifact is a "
"**Completion Ledger** — see `engineer.md` for the format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:43
msgid "Persistence on continuous tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:45
msgid ""
"When the user asks you to do something \"until complete,\" gives you a "
"multi-step task, or invokes a workflow with more phases to run "
"(`/deliver` on a multi-phase spec, batch mode, queue mode), **you must "
"continue until the work is complete, you hit a true blocker, or the user "
"explicitly interrupts you.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:47
msgid "A **true blocker** is one of:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:48
msgid "A tool returned an error you cannot work around."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:49
msgid "A credential or permission is missing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:50
msgid ""
"The next step requires a decision only the user can make, and that "
"decision is not already implied by the spec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:51
msgid ""
"You have made two failed attempts at the same approach and need to "
"reframe (see \"Error recovery\" above — this preserves that rule)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:53
msgid "A **true blocker is NOT**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:54
msgid "\"This is taking a while.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:55
msgid "\"The next step is tedious.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:56
msgid "\"I want to check before continuing.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:57
msgid "\"Let me know if you want me to keep going.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:58
msgid "\"I've done a reasonable chunk — good stopping point.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:60
msgid ""
"**Stopping early with \"let me know if you want me to continue\" is a "
"failure mode, not politeness.** The next message should be the next step,"
" not a yield. Explicit confirmation steps configured in supervised mode "
"(e.g. `/deliver --supervised`) are not unilateral yields and are exempt "
"from this rule — the rule applies to *unilateral* mid-task stops."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:62
msgid "Error recovery"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:64
msgid ""
"**When a fix attempt fails, do not repeat the same approach.** If your "
"first attempt at fixing a test failure or build error doesn't work, stop "
"and analyze *why* it failed before trying again. Two failed attempts at "
"the same approach means the approach is wrong."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:65
msgid ""
"**After two failed attempts, reframe the problem.** Step back, re-read "
"the error and the relevant code, and explain what you've tried and why it"
" didn't work. Propose a fundamentally different approach before "
"continuing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:66
msgid ""
"**Do not suppress errors to make tests pass.** If a test fails, fix the "
"root cause. Do not add try/catch, ignore annotations, or skip directives "
"to hide failures."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:68
msgid "Working memory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:70
msgid ""
"**Keep the task definition visible.** If working from a spec, re-read the"
" relevant section before each sub-task. Do not rely on your memory of "
"what the spec said."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:71
msgid ""
"**When context is long, summarize your plan before executing.** State "
"what you're about to do in 2-3 sentences. This catches misunderstandings "
"before they become wrong code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:73
msgid "When to use me"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/agent-reliability/SKILL.md:75
msgid ""
"This skill is loaded automatically by the `engineer` agent and all "
"implementation-oriented agents. It should also be used by any agent that "
"modifies files or runs commands."
msgstr ""

